---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import McpButton from '../components/McpButton.astro';
import CopyButton from '../components/CopyButton.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';

const mcpConfig = `{
  "mcpServers": {
    "kuyfi": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@kuyfi/mcp@latest"],
      "env": {
        "KUYFI_NETWORK": "stellar:testnet"
      }
    }
  }
}`;
---

<DocsLayout
	title="MCP"
	eyebrow="[ MCP · SOON ]"
	description="Reserved Model Context Protocol entry for Kuyfi — wire agents once the server package ships."
>
	<div class="hero-row">
		<McpButton variant="hero" href="#connect" />
		<span class="status">Status: stub · package not published yet</span>
	</div>

	<Callout type="info" title="Why this page exists now">
		<p>
			The marketing site and docs expose a stable <strong>MCP Connect</strong> affordance so
			future clients (Cursor, Claude, custom agents) can deep-link here. The npm package
			<code>@kuyfi/mcp</code> is a planned companion — do not treat the config below as
			live until this page’s status flips to <em>available</em>.
		</p>
	</Callout>

	<h2 id="connect">Intended capabilities</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><code>kuyfi_scan</code> — OSINT attack-surface reconstruction for a Contract ID</li>
		<li>
			<code>kuyfi_audit</code> — local Chaos Monkey campaign (explicit user confirmation;
			Testnet only)
		</li>
		<li><code>kuyfi_report_schema</code> — SecurityReport 1.0.0 field map</li>
		<li><code>kuyfi_signals</code> — finding taxonomy reference</li>
	</ul>

	<p>
		Remote paid scan may map to a read-only tool backed by <code>GET /scan/:id</code>. Chaos
		Monkey will remain opt-in and local-first.
	</p>

	<h2>Draft Cursor / Claude config</h2>
	<p>Copy this when <code>@kuyfi/mcp</code> is published:</p>
	<div class="config-block">
		<pre><code>{mcpConfig}</code></pre>
		<div class="config-actions">
			<CopyButton text={mcpConfig} label="COPY CONFIG" />
		</div>
	</div>

	<h2>Connect button contract</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Header + docs pages render <code>&lt;McpButton&gt;</code> linking here.</li>
		<li>
			Attribute <code>data-mcp-entry</code> marks the CTA for future JS enhancers (deeplink
			handlers, install modals).
		</li>
		<li>Visual language: yellow border, soft yellow fill — matches Install COPY CTA.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Until then</h2>
	<p>
		Agents should use CLI + <a href={withBase('/for-llms')}>For LLMs</a>:
	</p>
	<pre><code>npm install -g @kuyfi/kuyfi
kuyfi &lt;CONTRACT_ID&gt; --json</code></pre>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
	.hero-row {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 1rem;
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}

	.status {
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.78rem;
		color: var(--text-dim);
	}

	.config-block {
		position: relative;
		margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem;
	}

	.config-actions {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: flex-end;
		margin-top: 0.5rem;
	}
</style>
